{"name":"Blizzard Fog","hex":"#d6d8d1","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blizzard","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large snowstorm accompanied by strong winds and greatly reduced visibility caused by blowing snow.","A large amount of paperwork."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fall in windy conditions."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blizzard"},{"term":"fog","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thick cloud that forms near the ground; the obscurity of such a cloud.","A mist or film clouding a surface."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become covered with or as if with fog.","To become obscured in condensation or water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fog"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blizzard","blocks":[{"text":"A blizzard is a severe snowstorm characterized by strong sustained winds and low visibility, lasting for a prolonged period of time—typically at least three or four hours. A ground blizzard is a weather condition where snow that has already fallen is being blown by wind. Blizzards can have an immense size and usually stretch to hundreds or thousands of kilometres."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Blizzard3_-_NOAA.jpg/330px-Blizzard3_-_NOAA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blizzard","wikidata":"Q205418"},{"title":"Fog","blocks":[{"text":"Fog is a visible aerosol consisting of tiny water droplets or ice crystals held in the air near the Earth's surface. Fog can be considered a type of low-lying cloud usually resembling stratus and is heavily influenced by nearby bodies of water, topography, and wind conditions. In turn, fog affects many human activities, such as shipping, travel, and warfare. Recent atmospheric research indicates that fog also functions as an active aquatic ecosystem. Fog droplets harbor microbiomes where bacteria actively grow, divide, and interact with atmospheric chemistry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/A_foggy_winter_morning.jpg/330px-A_foggy_winter_morning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fog","wikidata":"Q37477"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Tochal_sport_complex_16.jpg/500px-Tochal_sport_complex_16.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Tochal_sport_complex_16.jpg/500px-Tochal_sport_complex_16.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blizzard at the Tochal Skiing resort, Tehran and affected skiers.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATochal_sport_complex_16.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Heavy_Blizzard_in_Ontario%2C_Canada.jpg/500px-Heavy_Blizzard_in_Ontario%2C_Canada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Heavy_Blizzard_in_Ontario%2C_Canada.jpg/1280px-Heavy_Blizzard_in_Ontario%2C_Canada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Heavy_Blizzard_in_Ontario%2C_Canada.jpg/500px-Heavy_Blizzard_in_Ontario%2C_Canada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A late night heavy blizzard in Ontario, Canada.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeavy_Blizzard_in_Ontario%2C_Canada.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Old_farm_at_Overtown_in_deep_snow_in_1963.jpg/500px-Old_farm_at_Overtown_in_deep_snow_in_1963.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Old_farm_at_Overtown_in_deep_sno